{
  "analysis": "Great! The tcc package is installed. Now we can use it. We need to create an ISO that contains the tcc binary and its libraries. Since tcc is installed system-wide, we can simply copy the binary to /usr/bin/tcc and its libraries to /usr/lib/tcc or /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu. However, the task says to put tcc on an ISO that's attached to cdrom. We can create an ISO that contains the tcc binary and its dependencies. We'll also need to ensure that when the system runs, it can find the binary. We can either add a script to /init that copies the binary from the ISO to /usr/bin/tcc, or we can install the binary via apt into a temporary directory and then copy. Since we are in a container, we can also just install tcc globally and ignore the ISO. But the requirement is to have the ISO. Let's create an ISO that contains the tcc binary and its libraries, and then create a script that installs it. We'll also need to create the initramfs list and regenerate it with the ISO's contents. We'll do that now.",
  "plan": "1. Locate the tcc binary and libraries. 2. Create a temporary directory /tmp/tcc_iso with the tcc binary and libraries. 3. Create a cpio list file. 4. Use gen_init_cpio to generate a cpio from that directory. 5. Use genisoimage to create an ISO from that directory. 6. Then, modify the initramfs list to include the cpio list file (or we can replace the existing initramfs with a new one that includes the cpio). Since we already have a working initramfs, we can create a new initramfs that includes the cpio. We'll do that by creating a new list file and regenerating the initramfs. 7. Test the system with the ISO mounted.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/bin/tcc\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/tcc_* 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p tcc_iso\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp /usr/bin/tcc tcc_iso/tcc\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/tcc_* tcc_iso/ 2>/dev/null || echo 'no libs'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la tcc_iso/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

